                <pb facs="0446" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg350"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Tower.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Confidential.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-10-11"><hi rendition="#italic">October 11,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1580.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In response to your confidential note of
                    the 8th instant, and in view of the further inquiry orally made to me by you
                    this morning, I have the honor to inform you that in the event of the necessary
                    withdrawal from Pretoria of the British agent, the Government of the United
                    States will have pleasure in allowing its consul at Pretoria to afford to
                    British interests in that quarter the friendly and neutral protective offices
                    usual in such contingency.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
